## Context
Reported by the DOIfetch session (raid f9e483, 2026-10-29) through the inter-project protocol; causes as its team lead stated them, not re-verified here.
Sibling of 1345 (egg-info). Observed:
- gaze inside a coder left its review tree behind because a `build/` directory blocked cleanup; the
  tree's liveness lock then blocked a re-run for about 20 minutes;
- verify-gate force-removed its own worktree twice (DOIfetch PRs #25, #27) because a `.venv` left by
  its touched-tests step blocked a plain remove, which the skill forbids forcing.
Both block reviews or break the no-force rule.

## Scope
Decide per artifact: count it as regenerable in `worktree_residue` (as 1345 did for egg-info), or
have the step that creates it remove it. Keep hand-made files under an ignored `build/` protected.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A review tree holding setuptools `build/` output is removed by gaze's close, by test
- [ ] verify-gate removes its tree after touched-tests without force, by test
- [ ] The stale liveness lock no longer blocks a re-run of the same review
